  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1228 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nAn upper-level ridge over the Southwestern US is slated to break \ndown going into the work week in advance of a weak shortwave trough \nthat moves in from the Pacific. Over the Panhandles, meanwhile, \nexpecting northwesterly flow aloft with negligible precipitation \nchances amid a trend of warming temperatures. Expecting highs to be \nin the 80s across the Panhandles by Tuesday. \n\nWednesday and Thursday, the aforementioned shortwave trough will \ntrack into New Mexico and Texas as a positively tilted trough. The \ntrough of this trough is expected to stay to the west and south of \nthe Panhandles through the remainder of the work week which will \ncontinue the trend of negligible precipitation chances. Expecting \nhighs in the 80s to continue through the week. \n\nOperational and ensemble mean guidance shows a longwave trough will \ndip into the Western US this weekend, and although there is wide \nvariation on how the trough will evolve, it will impact our weather \nin some way that is to be determined. \n\nVanden Bosch",
